; Safe property for crossing_relu.nnet (computes f(x) = |x|).
;
; STANDARD VNN-LIB CONVENTION: the output assert below encodes the NEGATION of
; the safety property — the violation the verifier must rule out. The safety
; property is "Y_0 <= 2.0 for all x in [-1, 1]"; the asserted violation is
; Y_0 >= 2.0. On the box, f(x) = |x| lies in [0, 1], so the violation is
; UNSAT and a sound verifier proves the property (CROWN upper bound ~1 < 2).
; Expected verdict: verified (property_status safe, exit 0).
(declare-const X_0 Real)
(declare-const Y_0 Real)

(assert (>= X_0 -1.0))
(assert (<= X_0 1.0))

; Violation (negated safety property): the output reaches 2.0 or above.
(assert (>= Y_0 2.0))
